      "The next morning, Heidi was awakened early by a loud whistle. Running out of the hut, she saw Peter the goatherd standing with his flock of lively mountain goats, ready to lead them up to the high alpine pastures. 'Do you want to go with him, Heidi?' asked the grandfather. 'Oh, yes!' cried Heidi, clapping her hands with joy.",
      "The grandfather washed her face at the wooden water trough, packed a hearty lunch of bread and golden cheese into Peter's leather pouch, and told the boy to watch over the child carefully. Hand in hand with Peter, Heidi bounded up the steep slopes under the radiant morning sky.",
      "High upon the pasture, the grass was dotted with glowing blue gentians, yellow rock-roses, and fragrant purple thyme. Heidi ran from flower to flower, laughing with delight. Above them, a great golden eagle soared in wide circles against the deep blue heavens, screeching its wild cry into the mountain silence.",
      "When winter arrived, deep snow covered the Alm-hut right up to the windows. The grandfather built a sturdy wooden sled, wrapped Heidi in warm woolen blankets, and flew down the snowy slopes like a bird to visit Peter's poor blind grandmother in her small wooden cottage. Heidi sat by the old woman's side, reading comforting hymns and bringing cheerful sunshine into her dark world, winning the love of every soul in the valley.",
