      "Heidi ran back up the mountain and told her grandfather about the broken shutters and the cold drafts in the old woman's cottage. The silent, stern old Alm-Uncle said nothing, but the next afternoon he packed his heavy wooden carpenter's box with hammer, nails, and sturdy pine planks. He trudged down through the deep snow drifts to the grandmother's hut and spent the whole day mending the rickety doors, securing the roof beams, and making the little cottage warm and weather-tight.",
